{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "run": 4,
  "simulation_id": "sim-03",
  "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round1_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B014",
        "laureates": [
          "Francis Halzen"
        ],
        "citation": "for establishing high-energy neutrino astronomy"
      },
      {
        "ballot_id": "B045",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B036",
    "B012"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "This configuration recognizes two experimentally secured advances that have changed our access to nature: a new astronomical messenger through IceCube and a new regime of precision measurement through optical lattice clocks. B014 has passed beyond a single surprising observation to a durable observational field, while B045 has an unusually crisp conceptual and experimental lineage in Katori and Ye and has been independently reproduced at extraordinary precision.",
    "case_against": "The strongest reservation is attribution for B014: IceCube is a collaboration-scale achievement, so Halzen can only be defended after a stringent historical examination of leadership and indispensable contributions. For B045, the citation must make clear why the magic-wavelength lattice-clock advance is a discovery-worthy physical achievement rather than merely outstanding instrumentation.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "pearce-mark",
        "point": "Pearce argues that high-energy neutrinos opened a genuinely new and durable observational window, while warning that individual credit must be balanced against the IceCube collaboration.",
        "response": "I agree with the scientific force of the new messenger and with the attribution warning. That warning is not peripheral: the archival record must show that Halzen's intellectual and institutional role is sufficiently distinctive for individual recognition."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll regards optical lattice clocks as a mature transformation of precision measurement, with Katori and Ye as clear central pioneers.",
        "response": "I find this attribution notably stronger than in several broader platform candidates. I would nevertheless retain Johansson's qualification that the committee should frame the prize around the lattice-clock principle and its physical consequences, not simply ever-improving clock performance."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "pearce-mark",
        "point": "Pearce notes that WMAP transformed cosmology but asks whether later CMB measurements supersede or reinforce its distinct contribution.",
        "response": "This is why I move B036 from my initial first place to an alternative. WMAP remains a profound, mature achievement, but its mission-scale attribution and its precise distinctness from later CMB work deserve a more focused historical review before it displaces the two preferred parts."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the documented individual leadership in IceCube supports crediting Francis Halzen alone.",
      "Whether WMAP's distinct prize-defining contribution can be cleanly separated from later precision CMB missions.",
      "Whether the nanohertz gravitational-wave background has sufficient elapsed time for source interpretation and collaboration-scale attribution to stabilize."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
